## Recommended Mitigation Steps

To mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to adhere to the "checks-effects-interactions" (CEI) pattern. Update the state of your contract after all external calls are successfully completed.

For the case of the _withdraw function, the revised code would look like this:

'''solidity
// Transfer the amount
(bool success, ) = to.call{value: amount}("");
if (!success) {
    revert TransferFailed(address(0), address(this), to, amount);
}

// Update the contract balance
balance -= amount;
'''

Additionally, always prefer transfer or send over lower-level calls. In fact, call is potentially unsafe as it provides direct control to the caller over the execution of the call.  


