# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Access Control:

Implement an onlyOwner modifier to ensure that only the owner can upgrade the implementation address.
Ownership Transfer Mechanism:

Providing a function to transfer ownership to a new address, allowing administrative flexibility.
Event Emissions:

Emit events for significant actions such as upgrading the implementation address and transferring ownership to ensure transparency and traceability.


## Proof of Concept

error ZeroImplementationAddress(); is called, but need to be called error OnlyOwner();

After https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-05-olas/blob/3ce502ec8b475885b90668e617f3983cea3ae29f/registries/contracts/staking/StakingProxy.sol#L23 we need to describe address public owner; ---> event ImplementationUpgraded(address indexed newImplementation); ---> event OwnerChanged(address indexed previousOwner, address indexed newOwner);

Between https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-05-olas/blob/3ce502ec8b475885b90668e617f3983cea3ae29f/registries/contracts/staking/StakingProxy.sol#L31-L33 need to be describe  owner = msg.sender;

Also between https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-05-olas/blob/3ce502ec8b475885b90668e617f3983cea3ae29f/registries/contracts/staking/StakingProxy.sol#L37-L39 we adding   /// @dev Modifier to check if the caller is the owner.
    modifier onlyOwner() {
        if (msg.sender != owner) {
            revert OnlyOwner();
        }
        _;
    }

    /// @dev Upgrades the implementation address.
    /// @param newImplementation New service staking implementation address.
    function upgradeImplementation(address newImplementation) external onlyOwner {
        // Check for the zero address
        if (newImplementation == address(0)) {
            revert ZeroImplementationAddress();
        }

        // Store the new service staking implementation address
        assembly {
            sstore(SERVICE_STAKING_PROXY, newImplementation)
        }

        emit ImplementationUpgraded(newImplementation);
    }

    /// @dev Allows the owner to transfer ownership to a new address.
    /// @param newOwner Address of the new owner.
    function transferOwnership(address newOwner) external onlyOwner {
        require(newOwner != address(0), "New owner is the zero address");
        address oldOwner = owner;
        owner = newOwner;
        emit OwnerChanged(oldOwner, newOwner);
    }



## Tools
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Addeding access control with the onlyOwner modifier.
Implementing an upgradeImplementation function to allow only the owner to upgrade the implementation.
Addeding a transferOwnership function to enable the owner to transfer ownership.
Included event emissions for ImplementationUpgraded and OwnerChanged to ensure transparency.




